(11. Why This Design?) Tj
0 -1.0 TD
(The project separates concerns so each class has a focused responsibility. A single large method) Tj
0 -1.0 TD
(could do all of this, but it would mix filesystem operations, parsing, business rules, sorting,) Tj
0 -1.0 TD
(and presentation. That would make changes and tests harder.) Tj
0 -1.0 TD
(The collection choices also match the jobs: List preserves sequences, HashMap supports counting) Tj
0 -1.0 TD
(without ordering requirements, and LinkedHashMap preserves a deliberate output order.) Tj
0 -1.0 TD
(This is intentionally a small learning project. A production version might use a full CSV) Tj
0 -1.0 TD
(parser, immutable defensive copies in Rulebook, stronger validation, and more writer tests. The) Tj
0 -1.0 TD
(current design keeps the fundamental ideas visible.) Tj
